From dd947aa5aef370db7a70b52e8a4ce97f494e4fd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A9-project <dmayala@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:25:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] drm: add a9_eink, Hisense A9 E Ink display with
 in-kernel software TCON

An 824x1648 KMS device (shmem GEM, damage clips) whose plane updates are
turned into E Ink waveform drive frames by a byte-exact port of the stock
composer's software TCON (a9tcon, from the A9 repo's scripts/mainline/tcon,
copied unchanged). The 448x829 drive frames are scanned out through an
in-kernel DRM client on the msm card (DSI0 -> TC358767 -> panel). Waveform
tables come from request_firmware(hisense/a9-waveform.bin), extracted by
the user from their own composer binary.

Default is a dry run: frames are computed and hashed but nothing is sent
unless a9_eink.enable=1, and the panel and FP9929A keep their own gates.
Userspace ABI: the connector's eink sysfs group (mode 513/515/518/521,
black_threshold, white_threshold, contrast, force_clear, status).
